2026-08-18T22:30:17.4808803Z > 
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4809178Z > # Phase 18 is the package's exhaustive simulation/reporting harness, and the
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4809741Z > # structured-conversion contract is a generated 22,000-assertion audit. Keep
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4810292Z > # both in repository CI, but do not rerun them during routine CRAN checks.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4810649Z > #
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4811038Z > # The second group is a CRAN check-time budget. Measured on 2026-08-10 (receipts
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4811611Z > # in docs/dev-log/release/0.7.0-cran-gate/test-timings.csv): the CRAN lane ran
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4812185Z > # 1160 s locally and 29-30 min of `checking tests` on win-builder, far above
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4812750Z > # CRAN's ~10-minute incoming guidance. Seventeen files carried 747 s of that
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4813313Z > # 1160 s; excluding them leaves 413 s locally (~6.9 min), projecting to ~10 min
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4813997Z > # on Windows at the measured 1.50x local->win-builder factor.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4814311Z > #
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4814700Z > # These are statistical-validation suites -- bivariate association sandwiches,
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4815572Z > # the G4/G5 missing-response foundation, zero-one-beta, bivariate Gaussian, and
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4816153Z > # the profile-target matrix -- not "does the package install and work" tests.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4816732Z > # They still run in full in repository CI, where NOT_CRAN=true. Nothing is
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4817264Z > # deleted and no test is weakened; this only changes which lane runs them.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4817619Z > #
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4818005Z > # The patterns are ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored "zero-one-beta" also
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4818558Z > # matches test-missing-predictor-zero-one-beta.R, and an unanchored
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4819173Z > # "biv-gaussian" also matches test-missing-response-biv-gaussian.R -- neither is
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4819689Z > # intended, and both must keep running on the CRAN lane.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4820002Z > #
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4820410Z > # `^julia` excludes every test-julia-*.R file. That alone is NOT enough: CRAN-lane
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4821019Z > # files such as test-binomial-response.R still call engine = "julia" inside
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4821561Z > # expect_error(), and Workflow G now admits fixed-effect binomial into the Julia
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4822188Z > # bridge, so the call reaches JuliaCall::julia_setup() before any rejection.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4822810Z > # Ligges win-builder (2026-08-16/17) hung there for ~10448s even after #1061.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4823369Z > # Defense in depth: (1) this filter, (2) drm_skip_live_julia() in live tests,
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4823939Z > # (3) drm_julia_setup() hard-blocks the CRAN lane unless DRMTMB_JULIA_TESTS=true.
2026-08-18T22:30:17.4824426Z > # The full suite still runs when NOT_CRAN=true.
